    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0332" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/2038</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-09T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. Your 341, May 8. For Constantinople:</p>
                <p>Your [May] 2 in regard to difficulties made against departure from Turkey of
                    American men between 18 and 45. If the Turkish Government is in fact preventing
                    their departure the Department would be much embarrassed, inasmuch as it was
                    preparing to facilitate <pb facs="0333" n="249" xml:id="pg249"/> the departure
                    of unofficial Turkish subjects from the United States to Bergen on May 19 by
                    securing safe-conducts from the British and French Governments. Please so inform
                    Sublime Porte and cable reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
